<h1 class="page-title">Parkhaven Bridge Design</h1>

<p>
    <br> As part of a university course, I joined a multidisciplinary design team (Architects & Engineers) and contributed to the conceptual and structural development of a new pedestrian–cyclist bridge across Parkhaven in Rotterdam. The project involved a site analysis, integration of future municipal plans, and the creation of a green mobility corridor linking key urban areas. I worked on developing multiple bridge typologies and iterations. My responsibilities included structural analysis (moment/shear modelling, load cases, and stability checks), cross‑section development, and design refinement of the truss and arch system.
</p>

